From: Nilanka de Silva <nilankadsilva@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: name GMAC netdevs from openwrt,netdev-name

OpenWrt applies the DT property "openwrt,netdev-name" from userspace in
/lib/preinit/04_set_netdev_label, a one-shot pass over /sys/class/net at
preinit time. On the GL-BE14000 the whole mtk_eth_soc probe completes
only after the RTL8261C PHY has initialised (about 0.6 s after preinit
starts), so the 10G GMAC frequently registers after that pass, stays
"eth2", and drops out of the configured bridge.

Give the netdev its DT name before register_netdev, the way DSA honours
"label" for switch ports, so no userspace rename is needed.

Signed-off-by: Nilanka de Silva <nilankadsilva@gmail.com>
[backport to 6.12 from JiaY-shi's flint4-support branch]
Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -4598,6 +4598,20 @@ static const struct net_device_ops mtk_n
 	.ndo_select_queue	= mtk_select_queue,
 };
 
+/* OpenWrt: take the netdev name from the DT so it does not depend on a
+ * userspace rename pass that can run before this driver has probed.
+ */
+static void mtk_netdev_name_from_dt(struct net_device *dev,
+				    struct device_node *np)
+{
+	const char *name;
+
+	if (of_property_read_string(np, "openwrt,netdev-name", &name))
+		return;
+	if (!strchr(name, '%') && strlen(name) < IFNAMSIZ)
+		strscpy(dev->name, name, IFNAMSIZ);
+}
+
 static int mtk_add_mac(struct mtk_eth *eth, struct device_node *np)
 {
 	const __be32 *_id = of_get_property(np, "reg", NULL);
@@ -4743,6 +4757,7 @@ static int mtk_add_mac(struct mtk_eth *e
 	mac->phylink = phylink;
 
 	SET_NETDEV_DEV(eth->netdev[id], eth->dev);
+	mtk_netdev_name_from_dt(eth->netdev[id], np);
 	eth->netdev[id]->watchdog_timeo = 5 * HZ;
 	eth->netdev[id]->netdev_ops = &mtk_netdev_ops;
 	eth->netdev[id]->base_addr = (unsigned long)eth->base;
